1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:07,230
What else do you think we could add to the course program to help with this reading problem?
你们认为我们在课堂项目上可以加点什么来解决阅读问题呢？

2
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:10,270
There's not really anything because it's my problem.
没有什么，因为这是我的问题。

3
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:13,300
I remember we were given long articles to read.
我记得我们曾经要读长篇文章。

4
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:20,570
We didn't like that but now I realise that reading those long articleswas good preparation for the things I need to read now. 
我那时不喜欢，但是现在我意识到读长篇文章对于我现在的阅读是一种很好的准备。

5
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:31,330
Also,in class we regularly had speed-reading tasks to do, and we kept a record of our reading speed, so the teachers were encouraging us to work on that.
另外，我们在课上定期会有快速阅读要做，我们对阅读的速度计时，因此老师鼓励我们这样做。

6
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:35,850
That's true Spiros,but what we read could have been different.
没错，Spiros，但是我们读得本可以不同。

7
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:44,000
Sometimes in the English class I felt frustratedwhen I had to read articles about the environment or health or education, 
有时在英语课上，当我读环境、健康或教育的文章时，我总感到受挫，

8
00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:50,990
because I wanted to concentrate on my own field, but we didn't read anything about engineering.
因为我想专注于我的领域，但是我们读不到任何关于工程学的文章。

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,190
So,I think I wasted some time learning vocabulary didn't need
所以，有时我觉得我在浪费时间学一些我用不着的词汇。

10
00:00:55,200 --> 00:01:00,560
But surely the strategies you were taught for dealing with that vocabulary were helpful
但是教你处理词汇的方法肯定是有用的。

11
00:01:00,570 --> 00:01:09,240
Yes,but psychologically speaking, I would have felt much better working on reading from my own field. What do you think Spiros?
是的，但是从心理上说，我更喜欢读自己领域的文章。你觉得呢，Spiros？

12
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:14,060
I agree;that would have helped my confidence too and I would have been more motivated.
我同意，这也会提高我的自信心，使我更有动力。

13
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:19,300
It was good though that we could work on our own topics when we wrote the research assignments.
当我们写研究作业的时候，这对于我们研究的题目也有帮助。

14
00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:23,830
Okay,let's move on to writing now ...
好的，现在谈谈写作……
